"""Assemble Online Resource 1: new header + plan changes + retained sections (S1-S3, localisation,
earlier IDRiD-copy sensitivity analyses) + data-driven sections generated by phase35_esm1.py."""
import re, sys
old = open("ESM1.md", encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
gen = open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8").read()
def block(a, b): return "\n".join(old[a - 1:b - 1])
TITLE = "Retinal foundation-model versus ImageNet pretraining for deep learning grading of diabetic retinopathy: an external validation study"
hdr = f'''---
title: "Online Resource 1 — Supplementary methods and results"
subtitle: "{TITLE}"
author: "Pravin Raj E (Department of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Chennai Institute of Technology, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India; pravinraje.aids2024@citchennai.net; ORCID 0009-0000-2975-1631)"
date: "International Ophthalmology"
---

This file contains every analysis performed for the study that is not shown in full in the article. All numbers in sections S4–S9 are generated by script (`phase31_paper_numbers.py`, `phase35_esm1.py`; Online Resource 4) from the per-image predictions in Online Resource 3, the same source as the article's tables and text. Unless stated otherwise, intervals are 95% percentile bootstrap intervals (2,000 replicates, seed 42); Messidor-2 intervals resample examinations (S4); the internal set is the deduplicated APTOS internal test set (n = 692); IDRiD denotes the **official** 516-image Disease-Grading release. Section S11 contains analyses run before the official IDRiD release was obtained, which use a 455-image third-party copy of IDRiD (audited in S1); their Messidor-2 and APTOS results are unaffected, but their IDRiD results are superseded. Abbreviations: LP, linear probe; QWK, quadratic weighted kappa; ECE, expected calibration error; MSP, maximum softmax probability; PPV/NPV, positive/negative predictive value.

# S0 Changes to the analysis plan

| # | Original plan | Change | When and why | Where the original result is reported |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Third-party copy of IDRiD (455 images) | Official IDRiD release (516 images) | After the label audit in S1 showed missing images and changed labels | S11 |
| 2 | All 733 internal-test images | 41 images with a byte-identical duplicate in training/validation excluded (n = 692) | Duplicates inflate internal agreement and therefore the drop | S6 (second table) |
| 3 | Image-level bootstrap; worst-case design-effect bound for Messidor-2 | Examination-level bootstrap using the official ADCIS examination file | Fellow-eye errors are correlated (S4) | S11.1 |
| 4 | One training run per model (seed 42) | Mean over runs (RETFound full: 3; EfficientNet-B3 and LP: 4), two-level bootstrap | A second RETFound fine-tuning run (seed 43), trained to estimate run-to-run variation, gave a materially larger excess drop than the first; the change was made after that result was known. The extra EfficientNet-B3 and LP runs had been completed earlier as a sensitivity analysis; the third RETFound run (seed 44) was specified before it was trained. | Table 4 of the article; S6 |
| 5 | — | Crossed-recipe control (EfficientNet-B3 with the RETFound recipe; RETFound with the CNN recipe) added | To separate pretraining from fine-tuning recipe | S7 |
'''
s1 = block(10, 50)
s2 = block(50, 71)
s3 = block(71, 88) + "\n\n**Additional runs.** RETFound full fine-tuning seeds 43 and 44 (`C:\\\\dr_ckpts_full_seeds`), EfficientNet-B3 seeds 43–45 (`outputs/phase4_baseline`), RETFound LP seeds 43–45 (`C:\\\\dr_ckpts_seeds`) and the control runs (label smoothing, crossed recipes) used the same selection rule (best APTOS-validation QWK, patience 7); their exact command lines are in the launchers in Online Resource 4 and their per-image predictions in Online Resource 3.\n"
loc = block(524, 630).replace("# S9 Saliency", "# S10 Saliency")
sens = "\n".join(old[629:])
sens = sens.replace("# S10 Sensitivity analyses (IDRiD mirror)", "# S11 Earlier sensitivity analyses (run with the third-party IDRiD copy)\n\nThese analyses were run before the official IDRiD release was obtained and before the changes in S0; they are reported for completeness. Their IDRiD results are superseded by the main analysis.")
sens = re.sub(r"## S10\.(\d)", r"## S11.\1", sens)
sens = re.sub(r"\bnan\b", "n/a", sens)
open("ESM1_v2.md", "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n\n".join([hdr, s1, s2, s3, gen, loc, sens]))
print("ok")
